  {
   "text": "The spinner ring is designed in SlicerX and passes its plan check: a 19 mm bore, the band captured by end lips, and the core and band as two separate bodies with no fused joint. I have not sliced or sent it to the P1S.\n\nOnly the 19 mm bore came from you. These are my guesses, shown on the sheet for you to confirm:\n- Core outer diameter 23 mm, so a 2 mm core wall.\n- Core and band width 10 mm.\n- Band wall 2 mm.\n- Radial clearance 0.4 mm between core and band.\n- End lips 1 mm wide, with a 0.2 mm axial gap so the band spins without binding.\n\nThe design is in the open project as \"Spinner ring\". If you want a different width or wall, tell me and I'll rebuild it. When you're ready, I can slice it for the P1S with the 0.4 mm nozzle and queue it, but I won't send anything until you say so."
